    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-intro",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Authoring switches",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 520,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Authoring switches\n\n**A draft, for Michael to edit.** What a person, a template or an agent can set on a node or a graph to change how it looks or behaves, in one place.\n\n**One description, many readers.** Each switch below is a node, and the node carries its own description as data (`data.switch`: name, scope, type, default, valid values, effect, where it is written, where it applies). The words on each card are written from that data. The Properties panel, a template or an agent can read the same fields, so the list is not a second copy to keep up to date.\n\n**How the pieces fit.** The script API is generic (`updateNode`, `updateView`, `createNode`, `applyDeltas`), so any switch can be written by a Method that declares the effect that allows it. This page says what can be written and where; the API says how.\n\n**Checked.** Each row was read against the code. A \"none found\" under Panel means no control turned up, not that none exists."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-policy",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Properties and policies",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 760,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Properties and policies\n\nA **property** is something an author declares: `rotation: 45`, `visible: false`, `defaultHandle`. A **policy** is a rule that reads properties and decides what happens. Policies are written down so that an author can predict them, and are not switches.\n\n## Visibility is three questions\n\n1. **Does the node exist?** It is in the graph, or it is not.\n2. **Is it eligible in this mode?** The *type rule* answers: a root, face, glyph, import, export or method is plumbing, and plumbing is for editing. `showInBrowse: true` is the one override of this rule.\n3. **Is it shown?** `visible` answers: false hides it, true is the default and changes nothing.\n\n`visibilityRole` is an older way to say (2) and cannot override the rule; it is kept for Scripts that present a node.web surface.\n\n## The root handle\n\nThe root Port always exists. Whether its handle is drawn is a policy: **auto** draws it when the graph is open, pointed at, or a connection is being made; `root.handle` can force it on or off. The Port and its Handle are separate: hiding one does not remove the other.\n\n## Which view shows\n\n`semanticLevel` and `semanticZoom.resolution` describe a face. Which face a tile shows at a given size is the app's policy: by how large the graph is drawn (glyph, then summary, then detail), and for a node, by the camera's zoom. The thresholds are in `semanticPresentation.js` and `graphViewPresentation.js`; they are not switches."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-visible",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "visible",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1160
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## visible\n\nFalse hides the node while browsing. Editing always shows it. True never brings plumbing back: that is the type rule's to answer, and showInBrowse overrides it.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node |\n| Written at | `node.visible` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | true |\n| Valid | true, false |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | yes (\"Visible\") |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "visible",
          "scope": "node",
          "writtenAt": "node.visible",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": "true",
          "valid": "true, false",
          "effect": "False hides the node while browsing. Editing always shows it. True never brings plumbing back: that is the type rule's to answer, and showInBrowse overrides it.",
          "appliesIn": "browse",
          "panel": "yes (\"Visible\")",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-show-in-browse",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "showInBrowse",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 1160
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## showInBrowse\n\nBrings a root, face, glyph, import, export or method into browse mode, as on a primitive page whose subject is the root and the views. Overrides the type rule only; visible: false still hides.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node |\n| Written at | `node.data.showInBrowse` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | false |\n| Valid | true |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | this page |\n| Status | built, nothing uses it yet |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "showInBrowse",
          "scope": "node",
          "writtenAt": "node.data.showInBrowse",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": "false",
          "valid": "true",
          "effect": "Brings a root, face, glyph, import, export or method into browse mode, as on a primitive page whose subject is the root and the views. Overrides the type rule only; visible: false still hides.",
          "appliesIn": "browse",
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "this page",
          "status": "built, nothing uses it yet"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-visibility-role",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "visibilityRole",
      "position": {
        "x": 1280,
        "y": 1160
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## visibilityRole\n\nNames a node as plumbing or as content. Ignored for the types the rule hides; honoured only for a Script that names a node.web presentation. Do not use it to show a root or a face.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node |\n| Written at | `node.data.visibilityRole` |\n| Type | enum |\n| Default | by the node's type |\n| Valid | \"editor\", \"browser\" |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md, as a warning |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "visibilityRole",
          "scope": "node",
          "writtenAt": "node.data.visibilityRole",
          "type": "enum",
          "default": "by the node's type",
          "valid": "\"editor\", \"browser\"",
          "effect": "Names a node as plumbing or as content. Ignored for the types the rule hides; honoured only for a Script that names a node.web presentation. Do not use it to show a root or a face.",
          "appliesIn": "browse",
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md, as a warning",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-position-locked",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "positionLocked",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1820
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## positionLocked\n\nPins the node. A pinned ground is drawn in a layer of its own beneath every other node and is never stepped down to a smaller view.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node |\n| Written at | `node.positionLocked` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | false |\n| Valid | true, false |\n| Applies | edit, browse |\n| Properties panel | lock toggle in the editor |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md (ground) |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "positionLocked",
          "scope": "node",
          "writtenAt": "node.positionLocked",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": "false",
          "valid": "true, false",
          "effect": "Pins the node. A pinned ground is drawn in a layer of its own beneath every other node and is never stepped down to a smaller view.",
          "appliesIn": "edit, browse",
          "panel": "lock toggle in the editor",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md (ground)",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
