    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-view-scroll",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "view.scroll",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 3800
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## view.scroll\n\nThe view is one page that scrolls, like the page behind a focused graph; a tile or a portal shows its scrollbar, and the wheel scrolls it only there.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | face |\n| Written at | `node.data.view.scroll` |\n| Type | enum |\n| Default | unset |\n| Valid | page |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | no |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "view.scroll",
          "scope": "face",
          "writtenAt": "node.data.view.scroll",
          "type": "enum",
          "default": "unset",
          "valid": "page",
          "effect": "The view is one page that scrolls, like the page behind a focused graph; a tile or a portal shows its scrollbar, and the wheel scrolls it only there.",
          "appliesIn": "browse",
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "no",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-membrane-bounds",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "membrane.bounds",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 3800
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## membrane.bounds\n\nCrops the graph's window by hand and turns the automatic box off. Set by dragging the corner of the focused graph. Do not use it to fix clipping: move the hidden nodes inside the box instead.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | root |\n| Written at | `root.data.membrane.bounds` |\n| Type | { x, y, width, height } |\n| Default | none: the box around the visible nodes |\n| Valid | a rectangle |\n| Applies | edit, browse |\n| Properties panel | corner drag |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "membrane.bounds",
          "scope": "root",
          "writtenAt": "root.data.membrane.bounds",
          "type": "{ x, y, width, height }",
          "default": "none: the box around the visible nodes",
          "valid": "a rectangle",
          "effect": "Crops the graph's window by hand and turns the automatic box off. Set by dragging the corner of the focused graph. Do not use it to fix clipping: move the hidden nodes inside the box instead.",
          "appliesIn": "edit, browse",
          "panel": "corner drag",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-render-shape",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "renderShape",
      "position": {
        "x": 1280,
        "y": 3800
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## renderShape\n\nA hint about the node's outline.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | node |\n| Written at | `node.data.renderShape.kind` |\n| Type | enum |\n| Default | none |\n| Valid | see the panel |\n| Applies | browse |\n| Properties panel | yes |\n| Written down | AGENTS.md says not to use it in new graphs |\n| Status | built, discouraged |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "renderShape",
          "scope": "node",
          "writtenAt": "node.data.renderShape.kind",
          "type": "enum",
          "default": "none",
          "valid": "see the panel",
          "effect": "A hint about the node's outline.",
          "appliesIn": "browse",
          "panel": "yes",
          "writtenDown": "AGENTS.md says not to use it in new graphs",
          "status": "built, discouraged"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-auto-run",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "autoRunOnLoad, autoRunOnGraphChange",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4460
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## autoRunOnLoad, autoRunOnGraphChange\n\nRuns the Method when the graph loads, or when anything in it changes.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | method, script |\n| Written at | `node.data.autoRunOnLoad, node.data.autoRunOnGraphChange` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | false |\n| Valid | true, false |\n| Applies | runtime |\n| Properties panel | yes (the system nodes panel) |\n| Written down | no |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "autoRunOnLoad, autoRunOnGraphChange",
          "scope": "method, script",
          "writtenAt": "node.data.autoRunOnLoad, node.data.autoRunOnGraphChange",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": "false",
          "valid": "true, false",
          "effect": "Runs the Method when the graph loads, or when anything in it changes.",
          "appliesIn": "runtime",
          "panel": "yes (the system nodes panel)",
          "writtenDown": "no",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-allow-mutations",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "allowMutations, dryRun",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 4460
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## allowMutations, dryRun\n\nWhether the Method may write to the graph, or only report what it would write.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | method, script |\n| Written at | `node.data.allowMutations, node.data.dryRun` |\n| Type | boolean |\n| Default | false |\n| Valid | true, false |\n| Applies | runtime |\n| Properties panel | yes |\n| Written down | no |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "allowMutations, dryRun",
          "scope": "method, script",
          "writtenAt": "node.data.allowMutations, node.data.dryRun",
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": "false",
          "valid": "true, false",
          "effect": "Whether the Method may write to the graph, or only report what it would write.",
          "appliesIn": "runtime",
          "panel": "yes",
          "writtenDown": "no",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-switch-root-handle",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "root.handle",
      "position": {
        "x": 1280,
        "y": 4460
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 620,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## root.handle\n\nThe root Port's handle on a workspace tile, on the left, where a Portal lands. auto draws it when the graph is open, pointed at, or a connection is being made; shown draws it always; hidden never. The Port itself is there either way.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scope | root |\n| Written at | `root.data.root.handle` |\n| Type | enum |\n| Default | auto |\n| Valid | auto, shown, hidden |\n| Applies | browse (the workspace) |\n| Properties panel | no |\n| Written down | this page |\n| Status | built |"
        },
        "switch": {
          "name": "root.handle",
          "scope": "root",
          "writtenAt": "root.data.root.handle",
          "type": "enum",
          "default": "auto",
          "valid": "auto, shown, hidden",
          "effect": "The root Port's handle on a workspace tile, on the left, where a Portal lands. auto draws it when the graph is open, pointed at, or a connection is being made; shown draws it always; hidden never. The Port itself is there either way.",
          "appliesIn": "browse (the workspace)",
          "panel": "no",
          "writtenDown": "this page",
          "status": "built"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "authoring-switches-questions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Questions",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5120
      },
      "width": 900,
      "height": 360,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Questions\n\n- Should **showInBrowse** go on the root, the faces and the glyph of every primitive page now, or one page first?\n- Is **root.handle** auto the right default, or should a graph have to ask?\n- Where does the finished list live: a canon page, a glossary entry, or both?\n- Should the Properties panel be built from the `data.switch` fields? That is the step that makes this the one description."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-switches"
        }
      }
    }
